# The Pi build this executor depends on.
#
# temporalio/pi PR #4 (branch moe/turn-steps), which stacks on PR #3, which stacks on PR #2:
#   #2 adds recordPrompt, prepareStep, step and resumeInterruptedTurn on AgentSession, which the
#      worker needs to drive a session one step at a time.
#   #3 adds pi.registerTurnExecutor, which the extension needs to make a session's own turns
#      durable.
#   #4 adds modelCall, runToolCall and sealStep, which split a step so each tool call is its own
#      unit of work, and hands the same three to an executor as turn.steps.
#   #4 also adds SessionManager.setWriteGuard, which is the only place a driver can be sure it
#      still owns the file: the write a model call ends with lands minutes after anything else
#      could have checked.
# None of it is in the published @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent, so the dependency is a build of
# the fork.
#
# Bump PI_FORK_REF when the PR moves, then re-run scripts/setup-fork.sh.

PI_FORK_REPO=https://github.com/temporalio/pi.git
PI_FORK_REF=3c3807a01f1723c6c0878d080305f1ea4cb77020
